[38;2;124;124;124m- $\widehat{f}(\lambda) \neq 0$ a.e.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe Riemann-Lebesgue lemma tells us $\widehat{f}(\lambda) \to 0$ as $|\lambda| [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\to \infty$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo for large $|\lambda|$, $|\widehat{f}(\lambda)|$ is small. This means for any [0m[38;2;124;124;124mfixed $r > 0$, the set $\{\lambda : |\widehat{f}(\lambda)| \leq r\}$ contains a [0m[38;2;124;124;124mneighborhood of $\pm\infty$, i.e., contains $\{|\lambda| \geq M\}$ for some $M$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSo $A_{R, r} = \{\lambda : |\lambda| \leq R, |\widehat{f}(\lambda)| \leq r\}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAs $R \to \infty$ with $r$ fixed, $A_{R,r}$ grows (it's increasing in $R$). As [0m
